# The api image needs the lockfile, the sources, and the tsconfigs. Nothing else.
#
# The exclusions matter more than they look: `COPY` sends the whole build context
# to the daemon, so without these the layer cache stores `node_modules` (hundreds
# of megabytes) and `.git` (the entire history) on every build — and, worse, a
# `.env` would be baked into a layer that someone can extract from the registry.

.git
.github
node_modules
dist
mock
tests
coverage
*.log

# Never let a developer's local secret file reach the daemon.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Docs and tooling that the image does not need.
*.md
!package.json
.vscode
.idea
Dockerfile
.dockerignore